### Auto-select by language

Set your OVOS language to `gl-ES` and leave `voice` unset — phoonnx will select a Galician voice automatically.

"tts": {
    "module": "ovos-tts-plugin-pico"
 }

The voice corresponds to a language code. OVOS auto-detects it from the global config.

You can also set it explicitly to one of `"de-DE", "es-ES", "fr-FR", "it-IT", "en-US"`:

  "tts": {
    "module": "ovos-tts-plugin-pico",
    "ovos-tts-plugin-pico": {
      "voice": "en-US"
    }
 }

Replace the plugin module and key. Voice IDs use the `piper/<lang_code>-<name>` format:

**Before:**
"tts": {
  "module": "ovos-tts-plugin-piper",
  "ovos-tts-plugin-piper": {
    "voice": "alan-low"
  }
}

**After:**
"tts": {
  "module": "ovos-tts-plugin-phoonnx",
  "ovos-tts-plugin-phoonnx": {
    "voice": "piper/en_GB-alan-low"
  }
}

