### Transformer pipelines

The server can run OVOS transformer plugins around synthesis, on every endpoint (native, vendor-compat, websocket, MCP/UTCP). **Dialog transformers** rewrite the text before synthesis, and **tts transformers** post-process the audio. Enable them with the standard mycroft.conf sections:

{
  "dialog_transformers": {
    "ovos-dialog-transformer-openai-plugin": {"rewrite_prompt": "reply in a cheerful tone"}
  },
  "tts_transformers": {…

This plugin is **enabled by default** in `ovos-config` alongside the other standard utterance transformers:

"utterance_transformers": {
    "ovos-utterance-normalizer": {},
    "ovos-utterance-plugin-cancel": {},
    "ovos-utterance-corrections-plugin": {}
}

To disable it, add `"enable": false` to your config:

"utterance_transformers": {
    "ovos-utterance-plugin-cancel": {"enable": false}
}

Set the plugin as the VAD engine in the OpenVoiceOS configuration:

{
  "listener": {
